# The game travels with the port that reads it - see reconstruct/. Its authors
# put it in the public domain in its own documentation, asking only that it not
# be put to commercial use without their agreement.
#
# popcorn/ stays out: it is the working copy the Python tools read, and the
# copy that matters is the one beside the binary that needs it. Two of the same
# bytes in one repository is one too many.
popcorn/
game/
*.hsc
*.bat

# A build product: recovered from popcorn.exe in a second by
# unpack_popcorn.py, so carrying a second copy of the same bytes serves
# nothing.
popcorn.unpacked.exe
snapshots/
*.snap
debug/
*.png
*.wav

# One-shot edit scripts, per docs/notes/editing-conventions.md
edit_*.py

venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.o

# Built by reconstruct/
reconstruct/popcorn
reconstruct/popcorn-dev
coverage.bin

# The ralph loop's own session state, not project content.
.claude/ralph-loop.local.md

# uv keeps its environment here.
.venv/
uv-cache/
